          "content": "Based on my exploration, here's the project structure breakdown:\n\n## Project Structure Overview\n\nThis is a **React-based AI-powered UI transformation assistant** built with Vite and TypeScript. The app helps users transform UI designs by comparing before/after images and generating code.\n\n### Core Files\n- **`App.tsx`** - Main application component with state management\n- **`index.tsx`** - React app entry point\n- **`index.html`** - HTML template\n- **`types.ts`** - TypeScript type definitions (TechStack enum)\n- **`constants.ts`** - Configuration constants (supported tech stacks)\n\n### Components Directory (`/components/`)\n- **`Header.tsx`** - App header component\n- **`ImageUploader.tsx`** - Handles before/after image uploads\n- **`StackSelector.tsx`** - Technology stack selection dropdown\n- **`ResultDisplay.tsx`** - Shows AI-generated transformation results\n- **`InputTabs.tsx`** - Tab interface for different input methods\n- **`InstructionsInput.tsx`** - Additional instructions input field\n- **`CodeManager.tsx`** - Manages code file inputs\n- **`CodeInput.tsx`** - Code input component (currently empty)\n- **`icons.tsx`** - SVG icon components\n\n### Services Directory (`/services/`)\n- **`geminiService.ts`** - Integration with Google's Gemini AI API for UI analysis\n\n### Configuration Files\n- **`package.json`** - Dependencies and scripts\n- **`vite.config.ts`** - Vite build configuration\n- **`tsconfig.json`** - TypeScript configuration\n- **`.env.local`** - Environment variables (Gemini API key)\n\n### Key Features\n1. **Multi-stack support**: React, Vue, Angular, Svelte, Flutter, SwiftUI, etc.\n2. **Image-based analysis**: Upload before/after UI screenshots\n3. **AI-powered transformation**: Uses Gemini AI to analyze differences and generate code\n4. **Code management**: Handle multiple code files\n5. **Additional instructions**: Custom transformation requirements\n\n### Technology Stack\n- **Frontend**: React 19 + TypeScript + Vite\n- **AI Service**: Google Gemini AI\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS (based on supported stacks)\n- **Code highlighting**: highlight.js\n- **Markdown parsing**: marked\n\nThe app follows a clean component-based architecture with clear separation of concerns between UI components, services, and type definitions."
